DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The PPCCII__IIOOVV__UUNNIINNIITT() method is called by the PCI Single-Root I/O Virtual‐
     ization (SR-IOV) infrastructure when the user requests that SR-IOV be
     disabled on a Physical Function (PF).  When this method is called, the PF
     driver must release any SR-IOV-related resources that it has allocated
     and disable any device-specific SR-IOV configuration in the device.

     This method will only be called following a successful call to
     PCI_IOV_INIT(9).  It is not guaranteed that PCI_IOV_ADD_VF(9) will have
     been called for any Virtual Function (VF) after the call to
     PCI_IOV_INIT(9) and before the call to PPCCII__IIOOVV__UUNNIINNIITT.

